According to the USCIS guidance, the following documents are required for I-485 filing:

1. Copies of every page of your passport or equivalent travel document (or valid explanation of why you do not have such a document) [Source: Document 5: Form I-485 Instructions (Adjustment of Status)]
2. Documentation of any departure from, and return to, the United States while in T-1 nonimmigrant status, including:
   A. Date of departure;
   B. Place of departure;
   C. Length of departure;
   D. Manner of departure (plane, boat, etc.);
   E. Date of return; and
   F. Place of return [Source: Document
